experiment.prespecified:
Fixed 2026-11-18, before any zoo result was read (borg-reborn-rs#551, #594). Pilot (RULES 16).
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's switch in its borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- the 16 non-Druid games play identical keys in both arms (only a Druid knows Fox Form); any difference is a defect.
Report per arm and per class:
- deaths and causes, final level, deepest level; paired rescued and newly killed against off;
- per Druid game: "# Fox Form: fleeing" casts, "# Fox Form: reverting for an item or a spell" and
  "# Fox Form: reverting to fight" notes, "You fail to concentrate" right after a cast, and blows struck as a fox
  ("You bite" / "You claw");
- Druid deaths: was the Druid a fox, fleeing, or changing back to fight in the last 100 messages?
Context: a local run on 29 Druid starts gave the same 3 deaths in both arms (CL1-2, before any flight), sum of CL
161 against 156, max depth 54 against 56. 2 Druids in classes-18 show safety only; survival needs the Druid tiers.
